cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "AURORA Agent (bioprism)"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "AURORA-NEURO"
repository-code: "https://github.com/AURORA-NEURO/aurora-agent"
url: "https://aurora-neuro.github.io/aurora-agent/"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-08-23
abstract: >-
  AURORA Agent is a Rust workspace (79 crates) implementing the FIBER
  decision-context compiler: a typed decision query is compiled into the
  smallest decision-sufficient evidence region, delivered as a Decision
  Section together with a Context Certificate stating exactly what was
  omitted and whether the omission could have changed the decision. On the
  shipped reference world of 761 facts, FIBER compiles the query to 11 facts
  (1.45%) and the deterministic oracle returns the correct verdict with all
  four leakage witnesses; on the same world a 5-hop graph walk and BM25
  select the identical eleven facts, and FIBER is distinguished only on a
  generated discriminating world. Certificate bytes are reproduced exactly
  by three implementations (a CPython reference, an eager Rust path, and an
  indexed store). The compiler is exposed as a command-line interface, a
  Model Context Protocol stdio server with 259 tools, and a local HTTP
  gateway. Research and developer infrastructure: it does not diagnose an
  individual, recommend treatment, triage care, enroll participants, or
  claim medical-device functionality.
